WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Basic Criteria for Defining a Defect Opportunity

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Welcome to this session on defect opportunities.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.100
What I'd like to do is briefly spend a little bit of time, and look at the criteria

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.300
for defining a defect opportunity.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:23.033
There's only three. They’re pretty simple. We’re going to cover them one at a time.

6
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:29.433
Criteria one. The Y variable must exist.

7
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:36.399
The Y variable must exist. A dependent variable must exist. That's pretty simple.

8
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:43.366
If you don't have a variable, it's not possible to realize a defect.

9
00:00:43.366 --> 00:00:48.099
If there is no critical to quality characteristic, there can be no defect.

10
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.466
If a defect cannot be realized, a defect cannot exist.

11
00:00:51.466 --> 00:00:56.366
If the defect cannot exist, then the circumstances are not favorable.

12
00:00:56.366 --> 00:01:01.899
Think of this, an opportunity is a set of circumstances favorable to an end.

13
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.266
In this case, favorable to a defect.

14
00:01:05.266 --> 00:01:10.266
Well, one of the circumstances is, the variable has to exist

15
00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:14.266
in order to be favorable to creating a defect.

16
00:01:14.266 --> 00:01:19.199
Therefore, if the circumstances are not favorable, there is no opportunity.

17
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.200
Criteria 2, the Y variable must be a scaled quantity.

18
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.600
If it is not a scaled quantity, right there, if it is not,

19
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.466
then a performance standard cannot be assigned. That simple.

20
00:01:33.466 --> 00:01:37.466
If you can't measure it, you can't put a standard to it.

21
00:01:37.466 --> 00:01:41.466
If there's no standard, you can't realize a defect.

22
00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:47.199
And then again, if a defect cannot be realized, a defect cannot exist.

23
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.200
And if a defect cannot exist, well self-evident.

24
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:58.766
Finally, the third criteria. The Y variable must maintain a performance standard.

25
00:01:58.766 --> 00:02:01.766
We just talked about that.

26
00:02:01.766 --> 00:02:05.699
So, three criteria. It's pretty simple.

27
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.800
Describes a defect opportunity. Let's put these in bright red,

28
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.200
so we can really kinda see them here, real good.

29
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.333
These are three important criteria for defining a defect opportunity.

30
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:24.333
One, the Y variable must exist.

31
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:30.633
Two, not only must it exist, it must be scaler. It must have scale to it.

32
00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:34.466
And three, on that performance scale, there has to be a standard.

33
00:02:34.466 --> 00:02:38.032
So, you gotta have a variable. You gotta have a scale. You gotta have a standard.

34
00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:42.799
If those three things are present, you got a defect opportunity.

35
00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.800
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
